      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Ridden,\n\nThis is a known limitation of the command (\u003dEC_REBOOT_COLD). The design decision is to let the callers take proper actions before cold reset.\n\nHave you tried to call EC_CMD_REBOOT_EC with cmd\u003dEC_REBOOT_COLD \u0026 flag\u003dEC_REBOOT_FLAG_ON_AP_SHUTDOWN? If so, how did it work differently from your expectation?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1054,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1057,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "722844e568ae1da5ef65cdb6ba1d3c72ebf2123e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1aaf003_2297931b",
        "filename": "common/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1057,
      "author": {
        "id": 1520632
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-16T00:40:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Becaues it was originally expected that when it `reboot at shutdown 4`, it would drop to G3 according to the spec powersequence and then do `EC reset`. But in fact, when drop to S5,it would directly do `EC reset`.",
      "parentUuid": "33c964a0_e6e72e2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1054,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1057,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "722844e568ae1da5ef65cdb6ba1d3c72ebf2123e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
